      "type": "numbered_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "SpringApplication.run",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " returns the application context after startup completes."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-boot-application-lesson-1-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Start the known application components",
        "language": "java",
        "description": [
          "`DemoApplication.java` starts the application.",
          "The included formatter, service, and configuration files define all application components used in this example.",
          "The project requires Java 17 or later and Maven."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "`DemoApplication` uses one `@SpringBootApplication` annotation to enable all three configuration features.",
          "Its configuration role allows bean definitions on the application class, although this example places the `Clock` bean in `AppConfig`.",
          "Component scanning finds `GreetingFormatter`, `GreetingService`, and `AppConfig` in `com.example.demo`.",
          "Spring processes `AppConfig.clock()` and registers its returned `Clock` as a bean.",
          "Spring supplies the formatter when it constructs `GreetingService`.",
          "Boot configures the web infrastructure because the included `pom.xml` supplies the Spring Web starter.",
          "The server starts without any application controller. This example registers objects but has no application endpoint."
        ],
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/GreetingFormatter.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Component;\n\n@Component\npublic class GreetingFormatter {\n    public String format(String name) {\n        return \"Hello, \" + name;\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/GreetingService.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\n\n@Service\npublic class GreetingService {\n    private final GreetingFormatter formatter;\n\n    public GreetingService(GreetingFormatter formatter) {\n        this.formatter = formatter;\n    }\n\n    public String greet(String name) {\n        return formatter.format(name);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/AppConfig.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport java.time.Clock;\nimport org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;\nimport org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;\n\n@Configuration\npublic class AppConfig {\n    @Bean\n    public Clock clock() {\n        return Clock.systemUTC();\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-boot-application-lesson-2",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Component search boundaries"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-boot-application-lesson-2-point-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Keeping "
        ],
        [
          "DemoApplication",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " above the application packages includes those packages in its default component search."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-boot-application-lesson-2-point-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Moving that class to another package changes the default search boundary."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-boot-application-lesson-2-point-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@SpringBootApplication(scanBasePackages = \"com.example\")",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " explicitly widens component scanning to that package and its subpackages."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-boot-application-lesson-2-point-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "This attribute changes component scanning only."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-boot-application-lesson-2-point-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JPA entity scanning and Spring Data repository scanning have separate rules, explained with their setup in the data-access lessons."
        ]
      ]
    }
